      "stem": "This is the Onboarding Assignment. Complete the four prompts in the assignment document: (1) describe the growth paths of two countries you compare in the widget (one growth miracle, one growth disappointment), (2) compute a rule-of-70 doubling time for one of them and explain what it means in lived terms, (3) summarize the essay you chose from the three options (Roser, Cowen and Collison, or Crawford), distinguishing one positive claim from one normative claim in it, and (4) write a short personal reaction describing what surprised you and what (if anything) shifted in your sense of the world. Target 600 to 900 words across all four prompts.",
      "model_answer": "A strong submission picks two countries with visibly different paths (e.g. South Korea vs. Argentina from 1960, or the U.S. vs. Niger from 1900) and describes the chart accurately, naming starting and ending levels and the rough multiple. The rule-of-70 calculation is correct and explicitly connected to lived experience: a 7 percent growth rate doubles real GDP per capita every 10 years, meaning the typical person is twice as materially well off as their parents were at the same age and four times as well off as their grandparents. The essay summary picks one of the three options and shows specific engagement: a fact, an argument, or a quoted phrase, not a generic gloss. The positive-normative distinction is clean (a positive claim describes the world; a normative claim says what should be), with one of each named from the essay. The personal reaction is honest and specific. It does not have to agree with the essay.",
