      "solution": "Rule of 70: doubling time (years) = 70 / growth rate in percent per year. 70 / 10 = 7 years. At 10 percent growth, living standards double roughly every 7 years. Sustained over 35 years, that is five doublings and a 32-fold increase from the starting level.",
      "review": []
