      "solution": "Rule of 70 in reverse: annual growth rate (percent) = 70 / doubling time (years). 70 / 25 = 2.8 percent per year. A country doubling every 25 years is growing at about 2.8 percent annually, roughly the long-run average for rich developed economies in the twentieth century.",
